// Docker-in-Docker, comprehensively: re-usable recordings of the Docker
// Engine API, for any language's tests to replay with no Docker daemon. A
// "comprehensive" suite of servirtium-vcr's pre-recorded/from-testcontainers
// (the README's "Pattern for comprehensive suites"; CouchDB is the pilot).
// Written for servirtium-vcr, not ported from testcontainers-go (whose dind
// module test only pings the inner daemon).
//
// The service is `dockerd` of docker:28.0.1-dind, listening on plain
// tcp://0.0.0.0:2375 with TLS off (testcontainers-ae's modules.dind), and a
// client is anything that speaks the Engine API: the docker CLI with
// DOCKER_HOST=tcp://..., a Docker SDK, testcontainers itself.
//
// PORTING: this file is the reference for what each tape holds; the tapes
// are the re-usable part. A port is a test in your language and test
// framework that makes the same requests, in the same order, against a
// Servirtium replay server loaded with the tape, and checks the same things.
// Any Servirtium implementation replays them. Every request here is plain
// HTTP/1.1 with these headers and no others:
//   User-Agent: testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)
//   Content-Type: application/json   (only when there is a body)
// Playback is strict about method, path (query string included, exactly as
// encoded here), the recorded request headers and the body (byte for byte:
// send the JSON bodies exactly as written in this file, no spaces), and fails
// a case whose recorded requests are not all made. Host, Connection and
// Content-Length are on the tapes but are transport headers, not compared.
//
// PORTING, the tape for each case: <case>.md beside this file, where <case>
// is the second argument of servirtium.recording(...) in that case. The
// cases are independent: each creates its own resources under fixed names
// (tcae-*), works in them and removes them on the tape, so any one tape
// replays alone and in any order.
//
// The API version in the path is FIXED: /v1.48/... (docker 28.0.1's maximum).
// A client library normally prefixes it itself; make yours send exactly
// /v1.48 (the docker CLI: `DOCKER_API_VERSION=1.48`; Go SDK: WithVersion
// ("1.48"); Python: version="1.48"). The unversioned /_ping and /version
// are taped as well, in the first case.
//
// Login: there is none. The daemon's plain-TCP socket has no authentication
// (that is why docker:dind logs a warning about it), so no tape carries a
// credential and no case is "logged in". A daemon behind TLS client
// certificates or a registry login (X-Registry-Auth) is a different set-up
// and out of scope.
//
// What varies between runs, and what the tapes do with it
// --------------------------------------------------------
// Every rule is registered in api_rules() below, with its reason; the
// "## [Recording rules]" table at the end of each tape lists them all and
// the interactions each touched ("none" where it did not). In short:
//   - normalized (each distinct value a stable {{docker-id-N}} token, the
//     same token wherever it recurs): the 64-hex ids Docker makes up for
//     containers, networks, endpoints and sandboxes, which show up in
//     create responses, inspect bodies, the paths inside them, and the 409
//     message of an image that a container uses. (Image ids and layer
//     digests are "sha256:<64 hex>" and are NOT touched: they are content
//     hashes, the same on every run for the pinned image.)
//   - collapsed (one constant; nobody sends them back): the daemon's own
//     time fields (a container's Created / StartedAt / FinishedAt, a
//     volume's CreatedAt, a network's Created, an image's LastTagTime, the
//     daemon's SystemTime) and its counters (/info's NFd, NGoroutines,
//     container and image counts, ID, Name), a process id, the sandbox
//     path, the short container id and an endpoint's random MAC, `top`'s process table, and the machine's memory and CPU
//     count.
//   - left out: the Date response header, as everywhere.
//   Everything else is deterministic and left alone, on purpose: the
//   engine's version numbers, the image's id and digest, the bridge
//   network's addresses (the cases fix their own subnet), exit codes.
//   Consequence: the tapes are for the host architecture they were recorded
//   on (arm64 here: busybox:1.36.1's image id and digest, /info's
//   Architecture, /version's Arch). A port asserts what a client uses
//   (status codes, the shape, names) and does not hard-code those.
//
// PORTING: in playback, a normalized value comes back as its token,
// verbatim: a container id is "{{docker-id-1}}". Treat every id as an opaque
// string (never assert its length or shape). These cases address resources
// by NAME (/containers/tcae-hello/start), as the CLI allows, so no token is
// ever sent back in a path.
//
// Pulling an image
// ----------------
// The first pull of an image streams progress events whose number depends
// on timing (how many "Downloading" lines the network produced), so a tape
// of it would differ run to run. Each case therefore makes sure the image
// is present BEFORE its recording starts (outside the recorder, live only),
// and the images case records a pull of an image that is already there: a
// short, deterministic stream ending "Image is up to date". A port's
// "already pulled" fixture is simply the tape of the case, or a stub for
// POST /images/create. The tapes do not record the first, downloading pull.
//
// Streams: a pull's progress is newline-delimited JSON, container logs are
// taped with a TTY (Tty:true) so they are the raw text, with CRLF line ends
// from the pseudo-terminal, kept on the tape and in replay: the assertions
// compare with CRs removed (lf() below), which works either way.
//
// In and out of scope
// -------------------
// In: _ping (GET and HEAD), version (versioned and not), info; images
// (pull of a present image, list, filtered list, inspect, history, tag,
// untag, prune); containers (create with and without a name, inspect, list
// with filters, start, wait, logs, stop, restart, pause/unpause, top,
// rename, remove, force remove, changes); networks (create with a fixed
// subnet, inspect, list with filters, connect, disconnect, remove);
// volumes (create, inspect, list with filters, remove); and the
// representative errors 304, 400, 404, 409 and 500 (a version too old or
// too new, a malformed body, a missing resource, a name already taken, a
// volume or image in use).
// Out: everything connection-level or streaming: attach, exec start, the
// `/events` stream, `stats` (a stream by default, and volatile numbers
// either way), `logs?follow=1`, pulls that download, image build and
// `images/load`, `export` and `get` (binary tar). Swarm, plugins, secrets,
// configs, `system/df` (sizes), and registry auth. Each could be a later
// case.
//
// Running it (from pre-recorded/from-testcontainers):
//   ae test dind/test_dind.ae                     container, no Servirtium
//   TCAE_VCR=record   ae test dind/test_dind.ae   write the tapes
//   TCAE_VCR=check    ae test dind/test_dind.ae   fail if a tape changed
//   TCAE_VCR=playback ae test dind/test_dind.ae   no container: the tapes
// The cases share one dind container (started on the first and removed at
// the end). It is privileged (that is what dind is) and, to run on a
// rootless Podman machine, in its own cgroup namespace
// (dind.dind_private_cgroupns(); Go's module uses the host's, which a
// rootless engine refuses). It pulls busybox from Docker Hub, so recording
// needs the network.

import std.spec
import std.string
import std.http.client
import testcontainers as tc
import testcontainers.docker
import testcontainers.testing
import servirtium
import modules.dind

const IMAGE = "docker:28.0.1-dind"

// The image the cases run inside the daemon: a pinned, tiny one.
const BUSYBOX = "busybox:1.36.1"

// The API version every versioned request carries.
const API = "/v1.48"

// The User-Agent this test's HTTP client sends, as an app's client library
// would (Aether's std.http.client adds none). Servirtium records what the
// client sends and adds nothing of its own.
const USER_AGENT = "testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HTTP helpers
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// One HTTP request: (status, body, error). ctype is the body's Content-Type
// (none when the body is empty).
fn http_send(method: string, url: string, ctype: string, body: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    req = client.request(method, url)
    client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
    client.set_timeout(req, 120s)
    if string.length(body) > 0 { client.set_body(req, string.bytes(body), ctype) }
    r, err = client.send_request(req)
    client.request_free(req)
    if err != "" { return 0, "", err }
    st = client.response_status(r)
    b = client.response_body(r)
    client.response_free(r)
    return st, b, ""
}

// The base URL of the current recording.
var api: string = ""

// A versioned Engine API request (path without the /v1.48): (status, body).
// A transport error fails the case.
fn dk(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}${API}${path}", "application/json", body)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// A request with the path exactly as given (the unversioned ones).
fn dk_raw(method: string, path: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}${path}", "application/json", "")
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// Percent-encode a query-string value (a `filters` JSON object): RFC 3986
// unreserved bytes stay, the rest %XX.
fn q(s: string) -> string {
    hex = "0123456789ABCDEF"
    out = ""
    b = string.bytes(s)
    i = 0
    while i < b.len {
        ch = b[i]
        keep = (ch >= 48 && ch <= 57) || (ch >= 65 && ch <= 90) || (ch >= 97 && ch <= 122) || ch == 45 || ch == 46 || ch == 95 || ch == 126
        if keep {
            out = string.concat(out, string.substring(s, i, i + 1))
        } else {
            hi = string.substring(hex, (ch >> 4) & 15, ((ch >> 4) & 15) + 1)
            lo = string.substring(hex, ch & 15, (ch & 15) + 1)
            out = "${out}%${hi}${lo}"
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return out
}

// A `filters` query value for one key and one value, percent-encoded:
// filt("name", "x") is {"name":["x"]} on the wire as %7B%22name%22....
fn filt(key: string, val: string) -> string {
    return q("{\"${key}\":[\"${val}\"]}")
}

// The body with its carriage returns removed (a TTY's logs end lines with
// CRLF; record and replay both keep them, and lf() makes the assertions
// indifferent to them).
fn lf(body: string) -> string {
    return string.replace_all(body, "\r", "")
}

// The create body of a container the cases use: the pinned image, a fixed
// hostname (otherwise Docker uses the first 12 hex of the container id, which
// varies), a TTY (so logs are raw text) and the command as a JSON array.
fn create_body(cmd_json: string) -> string {
    return "{\"Image\":\"${BUSYBOX}\",\"Hostname\":\"tcae-host\",\"Tty\":true,\"Cmd\":${cmd_json}}"
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The live daemon the cases share (record, check and off modes only)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

var shared_addr: string = ""
var shared_container: ptr = null

// The daemon's base URL, starting it on first use ("" on failure).
fn shared() -> string {
    if string.length(shared_addr) > 0 { return shared_addr }
    c, err = dind.run(IMAGE) { dind_private_cgroupns() }
    if c == null {
        spec.fail("dind starts: ${err}")
        return ""
    }
    shared_container = c as ptr
    spec.assert_ok(err, "dind starts")
    if err != "" { return "" }
    h, herr = dind.host(c)
    spec.assert_ok(herr, "dind host")
    if herr != "" { return "" }
    shared_addr = h
    return shared_addr
}

// Make sure the image is in the inner daemon, pulling it (and reading the
// progress stream to its end) if not. Live only, outside any recording.
fn ensure_image(addr: string) {
    st, _b, err = http_send("GET", "${addr}${API}/images/${BUSYBOX}/json", "", "")
    spec.assert_ok(err, "look for ${BUSYBOX} (not recorded)")
    if st == 200 { return }
    pst, pb, perr = http_send("POST", "${addr}${API}/images/create?fromImage=busybox&tag=1.36.1", "", "")
    spec.assert_ok(perr, "pull ${BUSYBOX} (not recorded)")
    spec.assert_eq(pst, 200, "pull ${BUSYBOX} (not recorded): ${pb}")
}

// Remove what an earlier failed run may have left behind (not recorded).
fn sweep(addr: string) {
    names = ["tcae-hello", "tcae-sleeper", "tcae-sleeper-renamed", "tcae-inuse", "tcae-dup", "tcae-member", "tcae-vol-user"]
    for n in names { http_send("DELETE", "${addr}${API}/containers/${n}?force=1&v=1", "", "") }
    http_send("DELETE", "${addr}${API}/networks/tcae-net", "", "")
    http_send("DELETE", "${addr}${API}/volumes/tcae-vol?force=1", "", "")
    http_send("DELETE", "${addr}${API}/images/tcae/busybox:test", "", "")
}

// Start a case: in a live mode, the shared daemon with the image present and
// no leftovers (none of that recorded); then the recording. Sets `api`;
// returns the recording handle, and ok = 0 when the case cannot run.
fn begin(case_: string) -> (ptr, int) {
    addr = ""
    if servirtium.live() == 1 {
        addr = shared()
        if addr == "" { return null, 0 }
        ensure_image(addr)
        sweep(addr)
    }
    base, rec = servirtium.recording("dind", case_, addr)
    api = base
    return rec, 1
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Recording rules
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn api_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // Docker's licence terms (UPSTREAM-TERMS.md) need no notice: Apache-2.0.

    // Ids Docker makes up: containers, networks, endpoints, sandboxes, and
    // the overlay2 directory names that appear in inspect. 64 lower-case hex,
    // not part of a longer run and not after "sha256:" (an image id or layer
    // digest, a content hash that is the same every run). Normalized, not
    // collapsed: the same id recurs (a create response, the inspect path
    // names, a network's container list) and a client may send it back.
    servirtium.normalize("(?<!sha256:)(?<![0-9a-f])[0-9a-f]{64}(?![0-9a-f])", "docker-id")

    // The daemon's own clock readings, in the fields that carry them: a
    // container's Created / StartedAt / FinishedAt, a volume's CreatedAt, a
    // network's Created, an image's LastTagTime, /info's SystemTime. Nobody
    // sends them back. Scoped by field name so that /version's BuildTime
    // (the engine build, which changes only with the image) stays. (An
    // image's own "Created" in `image inspect` shares a field name and is
    // collapsed too; its id and digest still say which image it is.)
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=\"Created\":\"|\"StartedAt\":\"|\"FinishedAt\":\"|\"CreatedAt\":\"|\"LastTagTime\":\"|\"SystemTime\":\")[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}(\\.[0-9]+)?(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})", "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z")
    // /info's identity and counters: its uuid, the host name (the dind
    // container's id prefix), file descriptors, goroutines, and the counts of
    // containers and images, which depend on what the other cases left
    // around. Each regex is anchored on its field name.
    servirtium.collapse("\"ID\":\"[0-9a-f-]{36}\"", "\"ID\":\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\"")
    servirtium.collapse("\"Name\":\"[0-9a-f]{12}\"", "\"Name\":\"dind-host\"")
    servirtium.collapse("\"NFd\":[0-9]+,\"OomKillDisable\":(true|false),\"NGoroutines\":[0-9]+", "\"NFd\":0,\"OomKillDisable\":false,\"NGoroutines\":0")
    servirtium.collapse("\"Containers\":[0-9]+,\"ContainersRunning\":[0-9]+,\"ContainersPaused\":[0-9]+,\"ContainersStopped\":[0-9]+,\"Images\":[0-9]+", "\"Containers\":0,\"ContainersRunning\":0,\"ContainersPaused\":0,\"ContainersStopped\":0,\"Images\":0")
    // The machine the daemon runs on: left to vary it would make a re-record
    // on another host a noisy diff, and no client sends these back.
    servirtium.collapse("\"NCPU\":[0-9]+,\"MemTotal\":[0-9]+", "\"NCPU\":1,\"MemTotal\":1")
    servirtium.collapse("\"KernelVersion\":\"[^\"]*\"", "\"KernelVersion\":\"kernel\"")
    // The short (12-hex) form of a container id, which Docker also uses as a
    // DNS alias (next to the fixed hostname, in a network endpoint's
    // DNSNames) and in the "image is in use" message. It is a prefix of an
    // id that is normalized above, but a regex cannot derive one token from
    // the other, so it is collapsed; nothing sends it back.
    servirtium.collapse("\"[0-9a-f]{12}\",\"tcae-host\"", "\"container-short-id\",\"tcae-host\"")
    servirtium.collapse("- container [0-9a-f]{12} is using", "- container container-short-id is using")
    // The container list's Created is Unix seconds (an image list's, which
    // has no Command or Ports beside it, is the image's own and stays).
    servirtium.collapse("\"Created\":[0-9]{10},\"Ports\"", "\"Created\":946684800,\"Ports\"")
    // Docker 28 gives every endpoint a random MAC address (an empty one, on a
    // container that has not started, is left as is).
    servirtium.collapse("\"MacAddress\":\"[0-9a-f]{2}(:[0-9a-f]{2}){5}\"", "\"MacAddress\":\"02:42:00:00:00:00\"")
    // The host pid of a running container (zero, for one that has exited, is
    // left as is: it says "not running").
    servirtium.collapse("\"Pid\":[1-9][0-9]*", "\"Pid\":4242")
    // The network namespace path of a running container.
    servirtium.collapse("/netns/[0-9a-f]{12}", "/netns/sandbox")
    // `top`'s process table: host pids and a start time, both of which vary.
    servirtium.collapse("\"Processes\":\\[\\[.*\\]\\]", "\"Processes\":[[\"root\",\"4242\",\"4241\",\"0\",\"00:00\",\"pts/0\",\"00:00:00\",\"sleep 300\"]]")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

main() {
    fw = spec.init()
    if servirtium.skip_if_no_engine(fw) == 1 { return spec.run_summary(fw) }

    api_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "Docker Engine API (dind)") {

        // PORTING: the daemon's identity and version negotiation.
        //   GET  /_ping               -> 200 "OK" (headers Api-Version: 1.48, Ostype: linux, Docker-Experimental: false, Builder-Version: 2, Swarm: inactive, Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate, Pragma: no-cache)
        //   HEAD /_ping               -> 200, no body
        //   GET  /version             -> 200 JSON: Version "28.0.1", ApiVersion "1.48", MinAPIVersion "1.24", Os, Components
        //   GET  /v1.48/version       -> the same
        //   GET  /v1.48/info          -> 200 JSON: ServerVersion "28.0.1", OSType "linux", Driver "overlay2", ...
        //   GET  /v1.99/version       -> 400 {"message":"client version 1.99 is too new. Maximum supported API version is 1.48"}
        //   GET  /v1.12/info          -> 400 {"message":"client version 1.12 is too old. Minimum supported API version is 1.24, please upgrade your client to a newer version"}
        spec.it("reports its version, health and info") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_its_version_health_and_info")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = dk_raw("GET", "/_ping")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /_ping")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "OK", "the ping body")
            st, b = dk_raw("HEAD", "/_ping")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "HEAD /_ping")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "", "no body for HEAD")
            st, b = dk_raw("GET", "/version")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /version: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"ApiVersion\":\"1.48\"", "API version")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Version\":\"28.0.1\"", "engine version")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/version", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /v1.48/version: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"MinAPIVersion\":\"1.24\"", "minimum API version")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/info", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /info: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"ServerVersion\":\"28.0.1\"", "server version")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"OSType\":\"linux\"", "OS type")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Driver\":\"overlay2\"", "storage driver")
            st, b = dk_raw("GET", "/v1.99/version")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a client version too new: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "client version 1.99 is too new. Maximum supported API version is 1.48", "too new")
            st, b = dk_raw("GET", "/v1.12/info")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a client version too old: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "client version 1.12 is too old. Minimum supported API version is 1.24", "too old")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: images. busybox:1.36.1 is already in the daemon (see "Pulling an image").
        //   POST   /v1.48/images/create?fromImage=busybox&tag=1.36.1 -> 200, newline-delimited JSON, last line {"status":"Status: Image is up to date for busybox:1.36.1"}
        //   GET    /v1.48/images/json                -> 200, a JSON array with RepoTags ["busybox:1.36.1"]
        //   GET    /v1.48/images/json?filters=%7B%22reference%22%3A%5B%22busybox%22%5D%7D -> 200, the same image
        //   GET    /v1.48/images/busybox:1.36.1/json -> 200, Id sha256:..., RepoTags, Os linux
        //   GET    /v1.48/images/busybox:1.36.1/history -> 200, an array
        //   POST   /v1.48/images/busybox:1.36.1/tag?repo=tcae/busybox&tag=test -> 201, no body
        //   GET    /v1.48/images/tcae/busybox:test/json -> 200 (the same image under its second name)
        //   DELETE /v1.48/images/tcae/busybox:test   -> 200 [{"Untagged":"tcae/busybox:test"}] (only the name goes; the image stays)
        //   GET    /v1.48/images/tcae/busybox:test/json -> 404 {"message":"No such image: tcae/busybox:test"}
        //   DELETE /v1.48/images/tcae/busybox:test   -> 404, same message
        //   POST   /v1.48/images/prune?filters=%7B%22dangling%22%3A%5B%22true%22%5D%7D -> 200 {"ImagesDeleted":null,"SpaceReclaimed":0}
        // Request bodies are empty.
        spec.it("pulls, lists, inspects, tags and untags an image") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("pulls_lists_inspects_tags_and_untags_an_image")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = dk("POST", "/images/create?fromImage=busybox&tag=1.36.1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "pull of a present image: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Image is up to date for busybox:1.36.1", "nothing to download")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/images/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /images/json: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"RepoTags\":[\"busybox:1.36.1\"]", "the image is listed")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/images/json?filters=${filt("reference", "busybox")}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "a filtered list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "busybox:1.36.1", "the filter finds it")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/images/${BUSYBOX}/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "inspect: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Id\":\"sha256:", "an image id")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Os\":\"linux\"", "the OS")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/images/${BUSYBOX}/history", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "history: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/images/${BUSYBOX}/tag?repo=tcae/busybox&tag=test", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "tag: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/images/tcae/busybox:test/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the second name: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"tcae/busybox:test\"", "it carries the new name")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/images/tcae/busybox:test", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "untag: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "{\"Untagged\":\"tcae/busybox:test\"}", "only the name goes")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/images/tcae/busybox:test/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "the name is gone: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "No such image: tcae/busybox:test", "no such image")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/images/tcae/busybox:test", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "untagging it again: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/images/prune?filters=${filt("dangling", "true")}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "prune dangling: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"SpaceReclaimed\":0", "nothing dangling")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: one container run to completion, addressed by name.
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/create?name=tcae-hello
        //          {"Image":"busybox:1.36.1","Hostname":"tcae-host","Tty":true,"Cmd":["echo","hello from the inner daemon"]}
        //          -> 201 {"Id":"{{docker-id-1}}","Warnings":[]}
        //   GET    /v1.48/containers/tcae-hello/json    -> 200, State.Status "created", Name "/tcae-hello", Config.Hostname "tcae-host"
        //   GET    /v1.48/containers/json?all=1&filters={"name":["tcae-hello"]} -> 200, an array of one, State "created"
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/tcae-hello/start   -> 204
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/tcae-hello/wait    -> 200 {"StatusCode":0} (blocks until the container exits)
        //   GET    /v1.48/containers/tcae-hello/logs?stdout=1&stderr=1 -> 200, "hello from the inner daemon\r\n" (raw stream: a TTY, no framing)
        //   GET    /v1.48/containers/tcae-hello/json    -> 200, State.Status "exited", ExitCode 0, Pid 0
        //   GET    /v1.48/containers/tcae-hello/changes -> 200 (null or an array: nothing the echo touched)
        //   DELETE /v1.48/containers/tcae-hello         -> 204
        //   GET    /v1.48/containers/tcae-hello/json    -> 404 {"message":"No such container: tcae-hello"}
        // Create's body is sent exactly as written (no spaces).
        spec.it("creates, starts, waits for, reads the logs of and removes a container") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("creates_starts_waits_logs_and_removes_a_container")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/create?name=tcae-hello", create_body("[\"echo\",\"hello from the inner daemon\"]"))
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "create: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Id\":\"", "the new container's id")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-hello/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "inspect: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Status\":\"created\"", "created, not started")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Name\":\"/tcae-hello\"", "its name")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Hostname\":\"tcae-host\"", "its hostname")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/json?all=1&filters=${filt("name", "tcae-hello")}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"/tcae-hello\"", "it is listed")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"State\":\"created\"", "as created")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-hello/start", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "start: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-hello/wait", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "wait: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"StatusCode\":0", "it exited with 0")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-hello/logs?stdout=1&stderr=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "logs: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(lf(b), "hello from the inner daemon\n", "what it printed")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-hello/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "inspect after: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Status\":\"exited\"", "exited")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"ExitCode\":0", "exit code 0")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-hello/changes", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "changes: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/containers/tcae-hello", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "remove: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-hello/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "it is gone: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "No such container: tcae-hello", "no such container")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: a long-running container, controlled.
        //   POST /v1.48/containers/create?name=tcae-sleeper {"Image":..,"Hostname":"tcae-host","Tty":true,"Cmd":["sleep","300"]} -> 201
        //   POST .../tcae-sleeper/start      -> 204;  again -> 304 (already started)
        //   GET  .../tcae-sleeper/json       -> State.Status "running", Running true, Pid collapsed to 4242
        //   GET  .../tcae-sleeper/top        -> 200 {"Titles":[..],"Processes":[[..]]} (the process table is collapsed)
        //   POST .../tcae-sleeper/pause      -> 204; GET json: State.Paused true; POST .../unpause -> 204
        //   POST .../tcae-sleeper/rename?name=tcae-sleeper-renamed -> 204; GET .../tcae-sleeper-renamed/json -> Name "/tcae-sleeper-renamed"
        //   DELETE .../tcae-sleeper-renamed  -> 409 (a running container is not removed without force) {"message":"cannot remove container \"/tcae-sleeper-renamed\": container is running: stop the container before removing or force remove"}
        //   POST .../tcae-sleeper-renamed/restart?t=1 -> 204 (stops it, 1 s grace, starts again)
        //   POST .../tcae-sleeper-renamed/stop?t=1    -> 204;  again -> 304 (already stopped)
        //   POST .../tcae-sleeper-renamed/wait        -> 200 {"StatusCode":137} (sleep as PID 1 ignores SIGTERM, so Docker kills it after the grace period)
        //   POST .../tcae-sleeper-renamed/start       -> 204 (a stopped container starts again)
        //   DELETE .../tcae-sleeper-renamed?force=1   -> 204 (kills and removes)
        spec.it("starts, inspects, pauses, renames, restarts, stops and force-removes a running container") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("controls_a_long_running_container")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/create?name=tcae-sleeper", create_body("[\"sleep\",\"300\"]"))
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "create: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper/start", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "start: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper/start", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 304, "start of a started container: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-sleeper/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "inspect: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Status\":\"running\"", "running")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Running\":true", "Running true")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-sleeper/top", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "top: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Titles\":[", "the column titles")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper/pause", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "pause: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-sleeper/json", "")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Paused\":true", "paused")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper/unpause", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "unpause: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper/rename?name=tcae-sleeper-renamed", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "rename: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-sleeper-renamed/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "inspect by the new name: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Name\":\"/tcae-sleeper-renamed\"", "the new name")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/containers/tcae-sleeper-renamed", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "remove while running: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "container is running: stop the container before removing or force remove", "running containers are not removed")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper-renamed/restart?t=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "restart: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper-renamed/stop?t=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "stop: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper-renamed/stop?t=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 304, "stop of a stopped container: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper-renamed/wait", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "wait: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"StatusCode\":137", "killed after the grace period")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-sleeper-renamed/start", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "start again: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/containers/tcae-sleeper-renamed?force=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "force remove: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: networks. The subnet is fixed so the addresses on the tape are stable.
        //   POST   /v1.48/networks/create {"Name":"tcae-net","Driver":"bridge","Labels":{"tcae":"1"},"IPAM":{"Config":[{"Subnet":"10.250.0.0/24","Gateway":"10.250.0.1"}]}}
        //          -> 201 {"Id":"{{docker-id-N}}","Warning":""}
        //   GET    /v1.48/networks/tcae-net -> 200, Name, Driver "bridge", IPAM.Config[0].Subnet "10.250.0.0/24", Labels {"tcae":"1"}, Containers {}
        //   GET    /v1.48/networks?filters={"name":["tcae-net"]} -> 200, an array of one
        //   POST   /v1.48/networks/create {"Name":"tcae-net"} -> 409 {"message":"network with name tcae-net already exists"}
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/create?name=tcae-member {"Image":..,"Hostname":"tcae-host","Tty":true,"Cmd":["sleep","300"]} -> 201; POST .../tcae-member/start -> 204
        //   POST   /v1.48/networks/tcae-net/connect {"Container":"tcae-member"} -> 200
        //   GET    /v1.48/networks/tcae-net -> Containers has the member, IPv4Address "10.250.0.2/24"
        //   DELETE /v1.48/networks/tcae-net -> 403 (an active endpoint: "error while removing network: network tcae-net id {{docker-id-N}} has active endpoints")
        //   POST   /v1.48/networks/tcae-net/disconnect {"Container":"tcae-member"} -> 200
        //   DELETE /v1.48/containers/tcae-member?force=1 -> 204
        //   DELETE /v1.48/networks/tcae-net -> 204
        //   GET    /v1.48/networks/tcae-net -> 404 {"message":"network tcae-net not found"}
        //   DELETE /v1.48/networks/tcae-net -> 404
        spec.it("creates, inspects, connects to and removes a network") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("creates_connects_and_removes_a_network")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = dk("POST", "/networks/create", "{\"Name\":\"tcae-net\",\"Driver\":\"bridge\",\"Labels\":{\"tcae\":\"1\"},\"IPAM\":{\"Config\":[{\"Subnet\":\"10.250.0.0/24\",\"Gateway\":\"10.250.0.1\"}]}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "create: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Id\":\"", "its id")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/networks/tcae-net", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "inspect: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Name\":\"tcae-net\"", "its name")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Subnet\":\"10.250.0.0/24\"", "its subnet")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"tcae\":\"1\"", "its label")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/networks?filters=${filt("name", "tcae-net")}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Name\":\"tcae-net\"", "it is listed")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/networks/create", "{\"Name\":\"tcae-net\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "the name is taken: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "network with name tcae-net already exists", "a duplicate name")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/create?name=tcae-member", create_body("[\"sleep\",\"300\"]"))
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "create the member: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-member/start", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "start the member: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/networks/tcae-net/connect", "{\"Container\":\"tcae-member\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "connect: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/networks/tcae-net", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "inspect with a member: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Name\":\"tcae-member\"", "the member is on the network")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"IPv4Address\":\"10.250.0.2/24\"", "its address")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/networks/tcae-net", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "remove with an active endpoint: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "has active endpoints", "active endpoints")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/networks/tcae-net/disconnect", "{\"Container\":\"tcae-member\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "disconnect: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/containers/tcae-member?force=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "remove the member: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/networks/tcae-net", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "remove the network: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/networks/tcae-net", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "it is gone: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "network tcae-net not found", "not found")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/networks/tcae-net", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "removing it again: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: volumes.
        //   POST   /v1.48/volumes/create {"Name":"tcae-vol","Labels":{"tcae":"1"}} -> 201 {"CreatedAt":..,"Driver":"local","Labels":{"tcae":"1"},"Mountpoint":"/var/lib/docker/volumes/tcae-vol/_data","Name":"tcae-vol","Options":null,"Scope":"local"}
        //   POST   /v1.48/volumes/create (same body)  -> 201, the same volume (create is idempotent)
        //   GET    /v1.48/volumes/tcae-vol            -> 200, the same
        //   GET    /v1.48/volumes?filters={"name":["tcae-vol"]} -> 200 {"Volumes":[..one..],"Warnings":null}
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/create?name=tcae-vol-user {"Image":..,"Hostname":"tcae-host","Tty":true,"Cmd":["true"],"HostConfig":{"Binds":["tcae-vol:/data"]}} -> 201
        //   DELETE /v1.48/volumes/tcae-vol            -> 409 {"message":"remove tcae-vol: volume is in use - [{{docker-id-N}}]"}
        //   DELETE /v1.48/containers/tcae-vol-user    -> 204
        //   DELETE /v1.48/volumes/tcae-vol            -> 204
        //   GET    /v1.48/volumes/tcae-vol            -> 404 {"message":"get tcae-vol: no such volume"}
        //   DELETE /v1.48/volumes/tcae-vol            -> 404 {"message":"get tcae-vol: no such volume"}
        spec.it("creates, inspects and removes a volume, and refuses to remove one in use") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("creates_inspects_and_removes_a_volume")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            vol = "{\"Name\":\"tcae-vol\",\"Labels\":{\"tcae\":\"1\"}}"
            st, b = dk("POST", "/volumes/create", vol)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "create: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Name\":\"tcae-vol\"", "its name")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Mountpoint\":\"/var/lib/docker/volumes/tcae-vol/_data\"", "its mount point")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/volumes/create", vol)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "create again is idempotent: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/volumes/tcae-vol", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "inspect: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Driver\":\"local\"", "the local driver")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"tcae\":\"1\"", "its label")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/volumes?filters=${filt("name", "tcae-vol")}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Name\":\"tcae-vol\"", "it is listed")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/create?name=tcae-vol-user", "{\"Image\":\"${BUSYBOX}\",\"Hostname\":\"tcae-host\",\"Tty\":true,\"Cmd\":[\"true\"],\"HostConfig\":{\"Binds\":[\"tcae-vol:/data\"]}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "a container that mounts it: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/volumes/tcae-vol", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "remove a volume in use: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "volume is in use", "in use")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/containers/tcae-vol-user", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "remove the container: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/volumes/tcae-vol", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "remove the volume: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/volumes/tcae-vol", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "it is gone: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "no such volume", "no such volume")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/volumes/tcae-vol", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "removing it again: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: the representative errors (the ones above are in their own cases too).
        //   GET    /v1.48/containers/tcae-nope/json   -> 404 {"message":"No such container: tcae-nope"}
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/tcae-nope/start  -> 404, same message
        //   GET    /v1.48/containers/tcae-nope/logs?stdout=1 -> 404, same message
        //   DELETE /v1.48/containers/tcae-nope        -> 404, same message
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/create?name=tcae-dup {"Image":"tcae/not-an-image:x"} -> 404 {"message":"No such image: tcae/not-an-image:x"}
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/create?name=tcae-dup {not json -> 400 {"message":"invalid JSON: invalid character 'n' looking for beginning of object key string"}
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/create?name=tcae-dup {} -> 400 {"message":"config cannot be empty in order to create a container"}
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/create?name=tcae-dup <the busybox body, Cmd ["true"]> -> 201
        //   POST   /v1.48/containers/create?name=tcae-dup <the same> -> 409 {"message":"Conflict. The container name \"/tcae-dup\" is already in use by container \"{{docker-id-N}}\". You have to remove (or rename) that container to be able to reuse that name."}
        //   DELETE /v1.48/images/busybox:1.36.1       -> 409 (a container uses it; unable to remove repository reference ... container {{docker-id-N}} is using its referenced image)
        //   DELETE /v1.48/containers/tcae-dup         -> 204
        //   GET    /v1.48/no-such-endpoint            -> 404 {"message":"page not found"}
        //   GET    /v1.48/images/tcae-nope/json       -> 404 {"message":"No such image: tcae-nope:latest"}
        // (the 400 for a body that is not JSON is sent as the exact bytes {not json)
        spec.it("answers the representative error statuses") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("answers_the_representative_error_statuses")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-nope/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "inspect a missing container: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "No such container: tcae-nope", "no such container")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/tcae-nope/start", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "start a missing container: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/containers/tcae-nope/logs?stdout=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "logs of a missing container: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/containers/tcae-nope", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "remove a missing container: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/create?name=tcae-dup", "{\"Image\":\"tcae/not-an-image:x\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "create from a missing image: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "No such image: tcae/not-an-image:x", "no such image")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/create?name=tcae-dup", "{not json")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a body that is not JSON: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "invalid character", "a JSON parse error")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/create?name=tcae-dup", "{}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "an empty config: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/create?name=tcae-dup", create_body("[\"true\"]"))
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "a valid create: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("POST", "/containers/create?name=tcae-dup", create_body("[\"true\"]"))
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "the name is taken: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "is already in use by container", "name conflict")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/images/${BUSYBOX}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "an image a container uses: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "is using its referenced image", "image in use")
            st, b = dk("DELETE", "/containers/tcae-dup", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "remove it: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/no-such-endpoint", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "an unknown endpoint: ${b}")
            st, b = dk("GET", "/images/tcae-nope/json", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "inspect a missing image: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "No such image: tcae-nope", "no such image")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }
    }

    if shared_container != null {
        e = tc.terminate(shared_container as *docker.Container)
        if e != "" { println("dind: removing the shared container: ${e}") }
    }
    return spec.run_summary(fw)
}
